:: Silver Stranger Meet
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
You leave the path and walk towards the bench. The silver-haired figure notices you before you reach them. They rise, wait until you are close enough to speak without raising their voice, then give you a small greeting.
<br><br>
<<switch $bodysize>>
<<case -1 0>>
	Even at your <<if $bodysize is -1>>miniature<<else>>tiny<</if>> height, they end up only a little taller than you.
<<case 1>>
	At your small stature, the two of you come to stand almost eye to eye.
<<case 2 2.5>>
	From your <<if $bodysize is 2.5>>tall<<else>>average<</if>> height, you find yourself looking down at them slightly. Up close, they are shorter than they first seemed.
<<default>>
	From your <<if $bodysize gte 4>>giant<<else>>large<</if>> frame, you loom over them. They look very small beside you<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>, enough that an unhelpful part of you briefly wonders whether they would be easy to pick up and move<</if>>.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
"There you are," they say. Once they have looked you over, they sit again and move one hand towards the empty space beside them. "Sit, if you like. I've been meaning to get a proper look at you without half the town getting in the way."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger Meet 1]]>><</link>>

:: Silver Stranger Meet 1
<<effects>>
Up close, the silver colour is even harder to ignore. Their hair is a bright silver-grey from root to tip, their skin is unusually pale, and their eyes reflect enough light that you can see a faint image of yourself in them. It makes their expression difficult to read; you can see where they are looking, but very little of what they think about what they see.
<br><br>
<<if $wraithIntro>>
	You have seen skin that pale before, deep in the water where the drowned ghost waits. The resemblance makes you look twice, though this person has colour in their lips and moves with none of the stiffness of a corpse.
	<br><br>
	"Not like your drowned friend, am I?" they ask before you say anything. They watch your face closely enough to see your frown. "You looked disappointed for half a second."
	<br><br>
	The comment makes you study them again. The comparison is already strange enough, but another detail keeps bothering you. Their clothes and face give you no clear answer as to whether they are a man or a woman. You look at their shoulders, their jaw, then their face again, and eventually decide that guessing will get you nowhere. Keep calling them <i>They</i>, then.
<<else>>
	Another detail keeps bothering you. Their clothes and face give you no clear answer as to whether they are a man or a woman. You look at their shoulders, their jaw, then their face again, and eventually decide that guessing will get you nowhere. Keep calling them <i>They</i>, then.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.bankHeist and $xchange.bankHeist.keptEarpiece>>
	Their attention drops briefly towards the place where you keep the earpiece hidden. "You kept something from the bank job. An earpiece that still connects you to someone on the other end."
	<br><br>
	They glance once more towards the hidden earpiece. "That sort of unfinished connection usually becomes my problem sooner or later. People keep one little piece because they think it is harmless, then discover that the person attached to it has been listening the whole time."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger Meet 2]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	"You've made quite a name for yourself," they say. "Enough people have talked about you, complained about you, or tried to use you that I would have heard about you eventually."
	<br><br>
	They give you a small smile. "I was curious whether the person matched all those stories."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger Meet 3]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Silver Stranger Meet 2
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $xchange.silverStranger.mickeyConfronted to true>>
"Mickey," they say.
<br><br>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	Your shoulders pull back before you can hide the reaction. One hand starts towards the hidden earpiece, but you stop it halfway and press your fingers against your side instead. "Please don't say that name."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You stop moving. Your hand twitches towards the hidden earpiece, then closes into a fist before it reaches it. "D-Don't say that name."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	Your hand starts towards the hidden earpiece before you catch yourself. You lower it again, straighten, and keep your voice controlled. "I'd rather you didn't say that name."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	You go still, then turn fully towards them. Your hand grasps the hidden earpiece. "Don't say that name again."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	Your hand snaps towards the hidden earpiece before you force it back down. Instead, you step closer to the bench. "Say that name again and see what happens."
<<else>>
	You freeze. Your hand twitches towards the place where you keep the earpiece, your fingers clenching before you can touch it. Part of you wants <span class="red">to crush it</span>; another part wants to grab the person who just said the name. "Don't say that name."
<</if>>
<br><br>
"The one behind the locked door," they continue, speaking as calmly as before. "The person who has been very careful to stay out of everybody else's reach."
<br><br>
You step towards them before you decide whether that is wise. "How do you know about them?"
<br><br>
"Because I pay attention to unfinished problems," the Stranger says. "Mickey left quite a few. People talk when they are frightened, angry, or trying to buy their way out of trouble. If the same name appears often enough, eventually I hear it."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger Meet 2.5]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Meet 2.5
<<effects>>
"That still doesn't tell me how much you know."
<br><br>
"No," they agree. "It doesn't. What matters is that Mickey has been an unresolved problem for a while. Normally, I would decide whether that problem needs removing before it grows."
<br><br>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	Your hands draw closer to your body. "Please. Just leave them alone."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You swallow, then force yourself to finish the warning. "If you touch them..."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	You keep your voice level even. "Then I suggest you leave them alone."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	You take another half-step forward. "If you touch them—"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
	You point at them. "Touch them and you'll have me to deal with."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
	You step close enough that they would have to look up at you. "Touch them and I'll make you regret it."
<<else>>
	Your body moves forward before the words are ready. "If you touch them—"
<</if>>
<br><br>
They raise one hand before you can finish. "Relax. I won't." They lower their hand again. "I would have to believe Mickey was still dangerous enough to justify the effort.
At the moment, they are hiding behind a locked door and relying on other people to act for them. I dislike giving someone that much importance when they have done so little to earn it."
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.silverStranger.introDone>>
	/* Later confrontation (already met and heard the trade intro): return to the hub. */
	<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger Meet 3]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Silver Stranger Meet 3
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $xchange.silverStranger.introDone to true>>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You keep your hands close to your sides and make yourself ask the question plainly. "Could you please just tell me what you want from me?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You hesitate, trying to work out whether asking will make things worse, then push the words out anyway. "What... what do you want from me?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	You straighten before speaking. "You've avoided the question long enough. What do you want from me?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	You face them directly. "Enough circles. What do you want from me?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
	You fold your arms. "Stop circling around it. What do you want?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
	You move a little closer. "Stop wasting my time. What do you want?"
<<else>>
	You force yourself to keep looking at them instead of checking the path behind you. "What do you want from me?"
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Mostly? To watch what you do next. Every time your name reaches me, the story is different. You get pulled into something unpleasant, survive it, then appear somewhere else dealing with a completely different kind of trouble. Most people settle into a pattern. You keep changing yours."
They reach into a hidden fold of their coat and take out a small capsule between two fingers.
<br><br>
"And I trade." They turn the capsule so you can see it properly. "If there is an <span class="lewd">X-Change pill circulating in this town, I can usually get it</span>, whether it is pink, blue, purple, or colourless.
I also carry premium stock that ordinary dealers never see, green pills that reverse the effects, and even the cheap unlabelled ones sold on street corners."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger Meet 4]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Meet 4
<<effects>>
They return the capsule to their coat. You hear several small cases shift against one another before the fabric settles.
<br><br>
"I don't plan to meet you here again. There are too many people walking through the park, and I would rather not have strangers watching every exchange we make." They look towards the water. "There is somewhere quieter across it.
You won't find that place marked on a map, but the docks are close enough for our purposes. Meet me there when you want to trade or ask questions."
<br><br>
After explaining where to meet them, they turn back towards you instead of letting the conversation end there.
<br><br>
"<span class="purple">I may ask you for a favour someday</span>," they say. "Nothing today. I simply prefer knowing where to find useful people before I need them."
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Park]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>

:: Silver Stranger
<<effects>>
The silver figure is waiting near the water in the same place as before. They notice your footsteps, turn away from the view, and give you a small nod as you come close.
<br><br>
<<if $daily.silverGenerous and !$daily.silverGaveFree>>
	"There you are," they say. "I'm feeling generous now, so choose carefully. What do you need?"
<<else>>
	"Back again?" They shift their attention fully towards you. "All right. What do you need this time?"
<</if>>
<br><br>
/* $xchange.silverStranger.asked counts how many questions have been asked (0-4).
   They come one at a time, in order: 1 Mickey, 2 Self, 3 Interest, 4 Route. */
<<if $xchange.bankHeist and $xchange.bankHeist.landryReported>>
	<<set _asked to ($xchange.silverStranger.asked || 0)>>
	<<if _asked lt 1>>
		<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask about Mickey|Silver Stranger Mickey]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<elseif _asked is 1>>
		<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask about them|Silver Stranger Self]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<elseif _asked is 2>>
		<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask why they take an interest in you|Silver Stranger Interest]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<elseif _asked is 3>>
		<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask what they know about your involvement|Silver Stranger Route]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if $xchange.colosseum and $xchange.colosseum.watcherAsk and !$xchange.silverStranger.colosseumAsked>>
	<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask why they watch you fight|Silver Stranger Colosseum]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $xchange.silverStranger.colosseumAsked and $fame.scrap gte 4000 and !$xchange.silverStranger.peakTalk>>
	<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Tell them there is nobody left to fight|Silver Stranger Peak]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if pillIsPermanent() and !$xchange.silverStranger.reversalSold>>
	<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask if a permanent transformation can be cured|Silver Stranger Reversal]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<pillicon>><<link [[Look at their wares|Silver Stranger Shop]]>><<set $silverShopView to "menu">><</link>>
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Docks]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Mickey
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $xchange.silverStranger.asked to 1>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You hesitate before bringing Mickey up again. "Have you... thought any more about them?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You choose your words carefully. "Have you given Mickey any more thought?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	You return to the subject of Mickey and ask whether their opinion has changed.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	You bring Mickey up again without trying to make the question sound casual. "Anything changed?"
<<else>>
	You ask whether they have thought any more about Mickey.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Nothing important has changed. Mickey is still where they were, still using other people whenever they can reach them, and still avoiding any situation where they would have to expose themselves directly."
They move one shoulder in a small shrug. "As long as that continues, I have no reason to interfere. If anything, the minor trouble they cause tells me who is still willing to answer when they call. That can be useful information."
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.bankHeist and $xchange.bankHeist.keptEarpiece>>
	Their eyes drop towards the place where you keep the earpiece. "You could still destroy that, you know. Keeping it means Mickey still has one possible route back to you, even if they never use it."
	<br><br>
	They make no move towards you after saying it. The suggestion is enough to make you think about Mickey's voice coming through the device again, and your fingers close around the earpiece before you have fully decided what to do.
	You pull it out, turn it over once in your palm, then squeeze until the casing cracks. <span class="red">The earpiece breaks between your fingers.</span>
	<br><br>
	The silver figure watches the pieces fall into your hand. "Humm. One less way for them to reach you."
	<br><br>
	<<unset $xchange.bankHeist.keptEarpiece>><<unset $xchange.bankHeist.hasEarpiece>>
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist and $xchange.bankHeist.earpieceCompromised>>
	"I did get something useful from that earpiece before it stopped mattering... to point me towards the people around them."
	They smile. "It may even be part of the reason I found you so quickly. A tiny device can leave a surprisingly long trail once enough people have touched the same problem."
	<br><br>
	<<unset $xchange.bankHeist.earpieceCompromised>><<unset $xchange.bankHeist.hasEarpiece>>
<</if>>
<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask something else|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Docks]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Self
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $xchange.silverStranger.asked to 2>>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
	You wait until there is a natural break in the conversation before asking what you should call them.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
	You ask their name quietly, unsure whether they will consider the question too personal.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	You ask what name, if any, they would prefer you to use.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	You finally ask what you are supposed to call them besides "the silver person at the docks".
<<else>>
	You ask their name.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Hmm?" They tilt their head, sending part of their long hair over one shoulder. "I don't give out names. If you need to refer to me, call me whatever helps you remember who you mean. I won't correct you."
<br><br>
That answer only gives you another question. You ask what they are, then point across the water and ask what sort of place they keep disappearing to when they leave town.
<br><br>
They look amused by the way you combine the questions. "Closer than you think, on both counts. You may already have passed people similar to me without realising it. Most know how to look ordinary when they need to."
<br><br>
You wait, but they do not offer a clearer explanation.
<br><br>
"As for the place across the water, you will find it when there is a reason for you to be there," they continue. "I could give you directions now, but that would only send you somewhere you have no business entering yet.
The town still has plenty for you to do, and I would prefer you alive while you do it."
<br><br>
<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask something else|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Docks]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Interest
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $xchange.silverStranger.asked to 3>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You take a little time before asking the question that has been bothering you. "Why do you keep taking an interest in me?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You ask what keeps bringing their attention back to you when there are so many other people in town.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	You ask why they have taken such a persistent interest in you.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	You ask what they keep seeing in you that is worth this much attention.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	You ask why they keep bothering with you when they could be watching somebody else.
<<else>>
	You ask why they continue coming back to you at all.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Because most people become predictable once you know what they want," they say. "If someone is driven mainly by money, safety, approval, or revenge, you can usually guess what choice they will make when that thing is threatened."
<br><br>
They turn towards you. "You are harder to reduce to one answer because sometimes you avoid trouble, while other times you walk straight into it. You can be frightened and still do something reckless, or furious and still stop yourself before you go too far.
That makes you difficult to predict, but it also means you can adapt when a simple plan stops working."
<<if $xchange.bankHeist and $xchange.bankHeist.heistComplete>>
	<br><br>
	"The bank proved that much. Whatever route brought you inside, you managed to keep moving after the situation stopped being simple."
	<br><br>
	"You know about the bank?" you ask.
	<br><br>
	"Of course I do." They give you a small, knowing smile. "Too many people were involved for something that large to remain private. I simply heard a more complete version than most."
<</if>>
<br><br>
"There is something I may need help with later," they continue. "<span class="purple">I do not know yet whether you are the right person</span>, so I am not going to hand you the details just because you asked nicely. But you are one of the few people I would consider."
<br><br>
<<link [[Let them keep talking|Silver Stranger Interest End]]>><<set $phase to "listen">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask more about it|Silver Stranger Interest End]]>><<set $phase to "ask">><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Interest End
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if $phase is "ask">>
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		You keep your voice careful. "Could you at least tell me what you would need me to do?"
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
		You hesitate, then ask anyway. "What would you need me to do?"
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"Then may I ask what kind of help you mean?" you ask.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
		"Then tell me what kind of job you're talking about," you say.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
		"So what is it? You keep mentioning this favour without saying what you actually want," you say.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
		You lean slightly towards them. "Enough hints. What would you want me to do?"
	<<else>>
		"What kind of help?" you ask.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	They raise an eyebrow. "Better. You finally asked about the job instead of asking another question about me."
	<br><br>
	You wait for the answer. They let the silence continue until it becomes obvious that they are enjoying your impatience.
	<br><br>
	"Nothing!" they say at last. "If I tell you now, you will spend the next week preparing for a situation that may never happen.
	I would rather see what you do when I ask for something without giving you months to prepare."
<<else>>
	You keep the next question to yourself and let them continue.
	<br><br>
	They notice. Their expression becomes a little less playful. "Oh? You can leave a question unanswered when pushing would gain you nothing. That matters more than sounding clever."
	<<npcincr Luchifen love 1>>| <span class="silverStranger">+ ???</span>
<</if>>
<br><br>
Whatever they mean, they clearly aren't going to explain it now.
<br><br>
<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask something else|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Docks]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Colosseum
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $xchange.silverStranger.colosseumAsked to true>>
You tell them you have seen them sitting under the old factory during your fights; always in the same general part of the stands, always alone. You never see them arrive with the crowd or leave with it afterwards.
<br><br>
They rest one hand on the back, smiling. "You want to know why I go? Hmm. Outside the ring, people have time to prepare themselves before anyone sees them. They decide when to smile, how confident to sound, how much fear to admit, and which answer will make them look best.
Most people do that so often they stop noticing it."
<br><br>
They tap one finger against the bench. "A fight gives them less time to manage all of that. At the start, a fighter can still perform for the room. They can grin after being hit, pretend their leg does not hurt, or act fearless because they want the other person to hesitate.
Once they are tired, hurt, frustrated, or frightened, they have to spend more attention on the person trying to hit them. That is when their automatic reactions become easier to see."
<br><br>
Their eyes move to you. "The reactions are different for everyone. One fighter may start backing away as soon as they think they could lose, while another becomes angry and attacks without thinking. Someone else may slow down and become more careful, or deliberately start hurting their opponent once fear turns into anger.
There are even people who keep trying to look calm while their hands are visibly shaking."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger Colosseum 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Colosseum 2
<<effects>>
A small smile appears. "You are interesting because I still cannot reliably guess which reaction I am going to get from you. You can look frightened and keep advancing, or look furious and suddenly stop yourself. Watching you fight tells me more than asking you what kind of person you think you are."
<<if $xchange.colosseum.quits gte 1>>
	<br><br>
	Their smile becomes thinner. "You did surrender once. I remember that night because the interesting part ended early. You decided you were finished, raised your hand, and left before I could see what you would have done if you had forced yourself to continue."
<<elseif $xchange.colosseum.rank gte 5>>
	<br><br>
	"You have also become much better than I expected," they add. "When I first saw you, I thought you would take a few bad defeats, decide the money was not worth the bruises, and stop coming. Instead, you learned how the place works and kept climbing. I had to revise my opinion."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You glance at them before asking whether they have ever bet on one of your fights.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You carefully ask whether they have ever put money on you.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	You ask whether they ever place bets when they come to watch you.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	You ask if they have ever bet on you.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	You ask if they ever put money on you, or if they really do spend the whole night sitting there purely to watch.
<<else>>
	You ask whether they have ever put money on one of your fights.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"No." The answer comes quickly. "If I had money on you, I would start wanting you to win. Then I would pay more attention to the result than to how you reached it. I would rather watch without needing either fighter to give me the outcome I paid for."
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask if they own the place|Silver Stranger Colosseum End]]>><<set $phase to "own">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Keep silent|Silver Stranger Colosseum End]]>><<set $phase to "drop">><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Colosseum End
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if $phase is "own">>
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
		You hesitate, then ask whether the Colosseum belongs to them.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile")>>
		You ask if they are involved in running the place.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		You ask whether they happen to own or manage any part of the Colosseum.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
		You ask them directly whether the place is theirs.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
		You ask if all this watching is easier because the place belongs to them after all.
	<<else>>
		You ask whether they own the place.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	They look genuinely pleased by the question. "Now you think I own everything... No. I do not own the factory, the bookmakers, the desk where you register, or the people who decide who fights whom."
	<br><br>
	They lift one finger before you can ask the obvious next question. "I do know people connected to it. That does not mean there is one owner waiting in an office for you to find. Places like that survive because responsibility is divided between people handling the money,
	controlling access, finding fighters, arranging matches, and dealing with whatever problems appear. Each person knows enough to do their part, while very few know enough to explain the whole operation."
	<<if $xchange.colosseum.story gte 4>>
		<br><br>
		"You have already been down the second stair and seen the cards by the doors," they continue. "So you have seen part of it yourself. If you remove one person, somebody else can still open the door, take the bets, arrange the matches, or collect the money.
		That is why attacking one convenient face does not make the system disappear."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	They lean back slightly. "You can keep asking who owns it if you like. Eventually, the question itself will tell the wrong person that you are trying to trace the chain."
<<else>>
	You decide not to ask anything else.
	<br><br>
	"Ah, yes, another silence. Questions can attract attention even when nobody answers them. If you ask people who controls a place like that, sooner or later someone will wonder why you need to know."
	<br><br>
	They look towards you again. "Knowing when to stop asking can keep you safer than getting one more name."
	<<npcincr Luchifen love 1>>| <span class="silverStranger">+ ???</span>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask something else|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Docks]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Peak
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $xchange.silverStranger.peakTalk to true>>
<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You tell them, with some disbelief still in your voice, that the fight board has run out of names above yours. The receptionist no longer writes proper odds beside you because nobody wants to bet against you.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You explain that there is nobody left above you on the board. Even the receptionist has stopped trying to find useful odds for your fights.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	You tell them that you have reached the top of the board. There is no higher-ranked fighter left to challenge, and the bookmakers have stopped finding people willing to take the other side of your odds.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	You tell them the board has finally run out. There is nobody ranked above you, and almost nobody wants to bet against you anymore.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	You tell them the Colosseum has run out of people worth putting in front of you. Your name is at the top, and the bookmakers can barely find anyone willing to bet on the other fighter.
<<else>>
	You tell them there is no name left above yours on the board. The receptionist has even stopped writing normal odds because nobody wants the other side of the bet.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"I know," they say. They are watching the tide move between the stones below the dock. "I was there when the board changed."
<br><br>
You wait for the usual teasing words, but they do not make one. Instead, they turn the subject back towards you.
<br><br>
"When you first started fighting there, I could understand why you kept returning. There was money to earn, a reputation to build, and always somebody stronger sitting above you. Every visit gave you a clear reason to come back again."
<br><br>
They turn their head towards you. "Those reasons are mostly gone now. You have more money than the purse can offer and nobody left to climb past, so you could stop going tonight and, as far as I can tell, your ordinary life would continue exactly as before."
<br><br>
Their eyes stay on your face while they finish the thought. "So if you go back down those stairs again, I will know you chose to. That interests me much more than watching you chase another rank."
<br><br>
<<link [[Say nothing|Silver Stranger Peak 2]]>><<set $phase to "listen">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask what that is supposed to mean|Silver Stranger Peak 2]]>><<set $phase to "ask">><</link>>

:: Silver Stranger Peak 2
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if $phase is "ask">>
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		You keep your voice careful. "Could you tell me what you mean by that?"
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
		You shift your weight before asking, "What do you mean?"
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"What do you mean by that?" you ask.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
		You fold your arms. "Then say what you mean."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
		"What's that supposed to mean?"
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
		You step closer to the rail beside them. "Stop talking around it. What do you mean?"
	<<else>>
		You ask what they are getting at.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	"I mean that choice tells me more than obligation does," they say. "That is all."
<<else>>
	You stay quiet instead of asking them to explain. They wait to see whether you will change your mind, then continue when you do not.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"A lot of people keep returning to places they hate because leaving would cost them something important. Debt, fear, work, a habit they cannot break, or another person who has power over them can all keep somebody in the same place.
If they stay because they have no practical way out, their staying does not tell me very much about what they want."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger Peak 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Peak 3
<<effects>>
They rest their forearms on the rail. "You are in a different position now. You can walk away from the Colosseum without losing your room, your income, or your place in town.
If you still return, then the return itself means something. You may enjoy the fighting or the feeling of winning, or perhaps you keep going back because you want to see whether anyone there can still surprise you.
I do not know which answer is true yet, which is why I keep watching."
<br><br>
They pick at a loose patch of rust with one fingernail, then stop and wipe the residue from their fingertip.
<br><br>
"People are tiring to read in ordinary conversation," they continue. "Most of them check my face before they answer. They decide what they think I want to hear, remove whatever sounds dangerous, then give me the safer version.
I have to spend half the conversation working out what was removed."
<br><br>
They turn towards you again. "You do much less of that. When something annoys you, you usually react before you have time to hide it: you frown before saying you are fine, or step closer before you make a threat.
If a question makes you uncomfortable, your body starts looking for a way out before your mouth decides whether to answer."
<br><br>
You become aware of your own posture and resist the urge to change it just because they pointed it out.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger Peak 4]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Peak 4
<<effects>>
They notice your movement too, and a small smile returns. "Exactly. I rarely have to guess which part of your answer is real. You make it visible before you can edit it. That makes being around you strangely easy."
<br><br>
The next part comes more slowly. Their hands settle against the rail instead of moving while they speak.
<br><br>
"I spend enough time around people who study every word I say because they want information, money, protection, or permission. I do not want more of that in the parts of my life I get to choose.
I would rather have someone who knows I can be difficult, gets annoyed with me when I deserve it, and still decides to come back later because they want to."
<br><br>
They look towards the town rather than at you. "Sometimes I imagine something very ordinary: a house with too many people in it, someone arguing in the next room over something stupid, dinner going wrong until another person takes over,
and children running through the hall after being told to slow down. Everyone talks loudly enough to be heard through the walls because nobody in the house has ever learned how to be quiet."
<br><br>
They slide one hand a little further along the rail before continuing. "In that house, nobody would be waiting for me to solve a problem or measuring every sentence I say.
It would be noisy and inconvenient, full of people who know exactly how irritating everyone else can be because they live together every day."
<br><br>
You tilt your head when you realise how long they have been talking.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger Peak 5]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Peak 5
<<effects>>
Every other conversation with them has been made of half-answers, teasing questions, and short pieces of information given only when they choose.
This time they have spoken for several minutes without making you drag each sentence out of them, and they have barely asked you anything in return.
<br><br>
They see you your expression and stop speaking. After checking your face, they seem to realise what you have just noticed.
<br><br>
"Oh, my!" They push away from the rail and put both hands behind their back. Their smile returns, but there is a brief awkwardness in the movement that was not there before.
"I think I said rather more than I meant to." <<npcincr Luchifen love 2>>| <span class="silverStranger">++ ???</span>
<br><br>
You wait to see whether they will explain any further. They only smile, making it clear that the conversation has reached its limit.
<br><br>
The silence lasts until they straighten and return to their usual casual tone. Then they ask whether you intend to fight again this week,
as though they had not just told you more about themselves than they have during every previous meeting combined.
<br><br>
<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask something else|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Docks]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Route
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<set $xchange.silverStranger.asked to 4>>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You ask how much they know about your part in everything that happened around the bank.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	You hesitate before asking how much they know about your involvement.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	You ask what they know about the way you became involved in the bank job.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	You ask them directly how much of your involvement they have managed to trace.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	You ask just how far they have been digging into your part in the bank job.
<<else>>
	You ask what they know about your involvement.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Enough to know where your part of the story started."
<<if $xchange.bankHeist.route is "gala">>
	They give you a knowing smile. "A gala. Formal clothes, expensive rooms, old family names, and a crowd where everybody is watching everybody else while pretending not to."
	<br><br>
	They angle their head slightly. "I am curious about one thing. Do you actually enjoy those events? The careful manners, the introductions, the little tests hidden inside ordinary conversation?"
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Say you rather enjoy them|Silver Stranger Route Gala]]>><<set $phase to "yes">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Say you can't stand them|Silver Stranger Route Gala]]>><<set $phase to "no">><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $xchange.bankHeist.route is "premium">>
	They think about it before answering. "You came in through the private side of things. Special orders, clients with enough money to avoid ordinary rules, and tests that were never meant for the public. That fits."
	<br><br>
	They look you over from head to foot, paying particular attention to anything unusual about your body. "I already suspected there was more happening to you than ordinary X-Change effects. After hearing where you were taken, I am even less convinced that 'ordinary' is a useful word for you."
	<br><br>
	"What are you implying?" you ask.
	<br><br>
	They smile without answering. "Only that this town has more ways to change a person than the ones pill packet."
	<br><br>
	<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask something else|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Docks]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	They look entertained. "Blackmail is simple, ugly, and very effective when the secret matters enough. Find something a person cannot afford to have exposed, tell them what you need, and suddenly they become much easier to direct."
	<br><br>
	They continue before you can answer. "I wonder how much you hated that part. Being controlled is one thing. Discovering that you can control somebody else can feel very different, especially when they have more money or status than you do."
	<br><br>
	Their smile becomes a little sharper. "Perhaps you will decide you like having that kind of leverage. Perhaps one day the people who once pushed you around will discover that you have learned the same methods."
	<br><br>
	They lean back against the rail. "If that ever happens, I expect it will be interesting to watch."
	<br><br>
	<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask something else|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Docks]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Silver Stranger Route Gala
<<effects>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if $phase is "yes">>
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		You give a small nod. "I think I do, yes."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
		You glance aside before nodding. "I... actually do."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
		You nod. "I suppose I enjoy them more than I expected to."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		You nod. "I suppose I do enjoy them."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
		You nod without hesitation. "Yeah. I like them."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
		You grin. "Of course I do."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
		You smile. "I do. Watching powerful people panic when something slips out of their control is half the fun."
	<<else>>
		You nod and admit that you enjoy the excitement more than you expected.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Their expression shifts into mild disbelief. "You really do?"
	<br><br>
	Their mouth pulls slightly to one side before they continue. "I cannot stand those rooms. Everyone is polite because they are supposed to be, while quietly deciding who has money, who has influence, who can be useful, and who can safely be ignored. Even a compliment can be chosen because somebody wants something from the person receiving it."
	<br><br>
	They glance at you. "If you enjoy that, perhaps you are better suited to it than I am. Just remember that people at those events notice mistakes. If you misread what somebody wants, they may smile through the whole conversation and only make the problem obvious after you leave."
<<else>>
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		You shake your head. "No. I don't enjoy them."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
		You look away and shake your head. "Not really."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
		You shake your head. "No. I'd rather avoid them."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		You shake your head. "Not in the slightest, I'm afraid."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
		You shake your head. "No. I can't stand them."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
		You pull a face. "Can't stand them."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
		Your mouth twists. "I hate them."
	<<else>>
		You shake your head. "Not in the slightest."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	"Neither can I," they say. "Too many people speaking carefully because they know one badly chosen sentence can travel through the room faster than they can correct it."
	<br><br>
	They rest one hand on the rail. "I still attend when I have to. Refusing the wrong invitation can attract more attention than quietly appearing, speaking to the people who expect you, then leaving. Sometimes being present causes less trouble than explaining why you stayed away."
	<br><br>
	They look back at you. "If you keep dealing with people from that world, you will run into the same problem sooner or later."
	<<npcincr Luchifen love 1>>| <span class="silverStranger">+ ???</span>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<socialiseicon "ask">><<link [[Ask something else|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave|Docks]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Shop
<<effects>>
<<if ($daily.silverBought or 0) gte 3>>
	The silver figure closes their coat before you can look through the cases again. "<span class="purple">That's enough for today</span>. Come back tomorrow. I would rather not empty half my stock into one person's pockets."
	<br><br>
<<else>>
They open the inside of their coat, revealing rows of small pill cases fitted into narrow pockets. There are more than you expected them to carry without the coat changing shape.
<br><br>
"<span class="teal">I carry what the town sells, plus a few things ordinary dealers rarely keep</span>. You pay more for the convenience, but I do not run out as quickly, and I have no interest in asking what you plan to do with what you buy."
<br><br>
<<if $silverShopView is "menu">>
	<<pillicon "xchangeGray">><<link [[Gray X-Change|Silver Stranger Shop]]>><<set $silverShopView to "gray">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<pillicon "xchangePink">><<link [[Pink X-Change|Silver Stranger Shop]]>><<set $silverShopView to "pink">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<pillicon "xchangeBlue">><<link [[Blue X-Change|Silver Stranger Shop]]>><<set $silverShopView to "blue">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<pillicon "xchangePurple">><<link [[Purple X-Change|Silver Stranger Shop]]>><<set $silverShopView to "purple">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<pillicon "pillcure">><<link [[Antidotes & Tests|Silver Stranger Shop]]>><<set $silverShopView to "support">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<pillicon "premium">><<link [[Premium & Clones|Silver Stranger Shop]]>><<set $silverShopView to "premium">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<pillicon "pill">><<link [[Suspicious pills|Silver Stranger Shop]]>><<set $silverShopView to "suspicious">><</link>>
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	<<link [[« Back to categories|Silver Stranger Shop]]>><<set $silverShopView to "menu">><</link>>
	<br><br>
	<<if $silverShopView is "gray">>
		<span class="gold">Gray X-Change</span>
		<br>
		/* Gray priced at £7,600 (base 475000 * 1.6 markup), above Landry's pub price of £6,000, but not too steep. */
		<<silverStockByPrefix "xchange_gray_" "xchangeGray" 475000>>
	<<elseif $silverShopView is "pink">>
		<span class="gold">Pink X-Change</span>
		<br>
		<<silverStockByPrefix "xchange_pink_" "xchangePink">>
		<<silverStockLine "xchange_sissy" "xchangePink">>
	<<elseif $silverShopView is "blue">>
		<span class="gold">Blue X-Change</span>
		<br>
		<<silverStockByPrefix "xchange_blue_" "xchangeBlue">>
		<<silverStockLine "xchange_butch" "xchangeBlue">>
	<<elseif $silverShopView is "purple">>
		<span class="gold">Purple X-Change</span>
		<br>
		<<silverStockByPrefix "xchange_purple_" "xchangePurple">>
	<<elseif $silverShopView is "support">>
		<span class="gold">Antidotes</span>
		<br>
		<<silverStockLine "xchange_antidote" "pillcure">>
		<<silverStockLine "xchange_antidote_forte" "pillcure">>
		<<set _silverAnti to []>>
		<<run (function () {
			(setup.pills || []).forEach(function (p) {
				if (!p || p.type !== "xchange" || p.subtype !== "anti-pill") return;
				if (typeof p.name !== "string") return;
				var m = p.name.match(/^SWP Anti-(.+) Pill$/);
				if (!m) return;
				if (m[1] === "portal" && !State.variables.portalPantiesEnabled) return;
				State.temporary.silverAnti.pushUnique(m[1]);
			});
		})()>>
		<<if _silverAnti.length gt 0>>
			<<for _t range _silverAnti>>
				<<set _antiName to "SWP Anti-" + _t + " Pill">>
				<<silverStockRaw _antiName 500000 "pillcure">>
			<</for>>
		<<else>>
			They check the pockets reserved for antidotes, then turn one empty palm towards you. "Nothing green today. Even I can run out when enough people buy the same thing at once."
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif $silverShopView is "premium">>
		<span class="gold">Premium &amp; Clones</span>
		<br>
		<<silverStockRaw "X-Change Premium" 1000000 "premium">>
		<<silverStockByPrefix "xchange_clone_" "premium">>
	<<elseif $silverShopView is "suspicious">>
		<span class="gold">Suspicious pills</span>
		<br>
		<<silverStockRaw "Suspicious Pink Pill" 2000 "pill">>
		<<silverStockRaw "Suspicious Blue Pill" 2000 "pill">>
		<<silverStockRaw "Suspicious Purple Pill" 2000 "pill">>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Step back|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Buy
<<effects>>
<<if $silverLastFree>>
	You reach for your money, but they put two fingers against the back of your hand and guide it away before you can pay. They press the small case into your palm instead.
	<br><br>
	"No charge. I told you I was feeling generous today. Take the gift before I change my mind."
	<span class="green">They gave it to you for free.</span>
<<else>>
	You hand over the payment. They slip the money into an inner pocket without counting it in front of you, then take the correct case from their coat and place it in your hand.
	<br><br>
	Through the clear section of the case, you can see the pill inside.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<set $silverLastFree to false>>
<<pillicon>><<link [[Look at their wares again|Silver Stranger Shop]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Step back|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Reversal
<<effects>>
<<set _cause to ($xchange.pill.permanentCause || "")>>
<<set _src to ($xchange.pill.choiceSource || "")>>
You tell them about the pill. The change has not worn off, and you don't think it ever will. It is permanent.
You ask if there is any way to cure it.
<br><br>
They look you over from head to toe, and the corner of their mouth lifts. They sound amused.
"Hmm. How did you manage that?"
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.pill.choiceEffect>>
	<<if _src.includes("Livestock")>>
		You tell them about the farm. You didn't behave in the milking stall, so Remy made you swallow a Choice pill as punishment.
	<<elseif _src.includes("Prison")>>
		You tell them about the prison. After Bailey dropped you off, an officer shoved a Choice pill down your throat and called it regulation.
	<<elseif _src.includes("Mansion")>>
		You tell them about Avery's mansion. Avery fed you a Choice pill and didn't listen when you objected.
	<<elseif _src.includes("Water Dragon") or ($waterDragonNest and $waterDragonNest.labChoicePill)>>
		You tell them about the lab. Harper gave you a Choice pill during the induction.
	<<else>>
		You tell them you took a Choice pill yourself. The packet came with a reversal pill, but you don't have it anymore.
	<</if>>
<<elseif _cause is "continue">>
	You tell them you kept taking Continue pills. The time kept adding up, and one day the change stopped counting down at all.
<<elseif _cause is "resistance">>
	You tell them you took a Resistance pill. It was meant to wear off, but it failed, and the change stayed.
<<elseif _cause is "pregnancy">>
	You tell them you got pregnant while you were changed. After that, your body stayed the way it was.
<<elseif _cause is "parasite">>
	You tell them about the slime in your ear. Once it had grown, your body stopped changing back.
<<else>>
	You tell them you don't really know. One day the change simply stopped wearing off.
<</if>>
<br><br>
They laugh quietly. "Of course." They lean back against the railing. "Yes, I can help.
I have a pill that undoes it, whatever made it permanent.
It will cost you <span class="gold"><<= formatMoney(setup.inflation.spendPrice(15000000, "blackMarket"))>></span>."
<br><br>
<<link [[Buy it|Silver Stranger Reversal Buy]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Say it's far too expensive|Silver Stranger Reversal Price]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Reversal Price
<<effects>>
"That's far too expensive," you say. "Why does it cost so much?"
<br><br>
They tilt their head. "Why not?"
<br><br>
They say nothing else. They only wait for your reply. You know that arguing with them will not change the price.
<br><br>
<<link [[Buy it|Silver Stranger Reversal Buy]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Not now|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Silver Stranger Reversal Buy
<<effects>>
/* Charged in the passage body, guarded by reversalSold, so a re-render can't charge twice. */
<<if !$xchange.silverStranger.reversalSold and setup.inflation.canAfford(15000000, "blackMarket")>>
	<<money -15000000 "blackMarket">>
	<<set $sexStats.pills["pills"]["Silver Reversal"].owned++>>
	<<set $sexStats.pills.boughtOnce to true>>
	<<set $xchange.silverStranger.reversalSold to true>>
<</if>>
<<if !$xchange.silverStranger.reversalSold>>
	You check how much money you have. It is not enough.
	<br><br>
	They see your face and smile. "Come back when you can pay. I will keep it for you."
<<else>>
	You hand over the money. They put it into an inner pocket without counting it,
	then take a small case from their coat and put it in your hand.
	<span class="green">Inside is a single silver pill.</span>
	<br><br>
	"Take it when you are ready. But do not come back asking for another. I will not sell you one again."
	They smile. "<span class="silverStranger">Unless you can convince me, perhaps?</span>"
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Silver Stranger]]>><</link>>
<br>
